put('comment-1237.md',ctx+'''Add the exact W02 preparation-family extension `W02-F-IRON-STOCK-DUPLICATE` (`w02-external-b-004`), cases53/176. The [DSMZ718 recipe](https://www.dsmz.de/microorganisms/medium/pdf/DSMZ_Medium718.pdf) (SHA256 `09faeca86ec0358bcdc3b5674e2323ac61c3ca554a9323bb09eb6f06fa6feb1c`) and [DSMZ399 recipe](https://www.dsmz.de/microorganisms/medium/pdf/DSMZ_Medium399.pdf) (`29f9f4df24231ba04f8113f3f7b6d8fd82b186c000608627ad02905808ae7ed0`) both state the literal seven-water ferrous ammonium sulfate stock at0.1%w/v,2mL receiving dose. One candidate expresses1g/L, which is the same stated strength.\n\n'''+table(['a2-proposal-dsmz718-ferrous-ammonium-sulfate-stock','c2-proposal-ferrous-ammonium-heptahydrate-stock'])+'''\nReconcile the overlapping supported partial-preparation scope into one justified nominal candidate or establish a positive material distinction before co-installation. Do not infer complete formulation equivalence from the same listed solute/strength; unknown solvent/batch details are neither proof of equality nor disjointness. Preserve both exact source/case lineages and the literal seven waters without silently converting to conventional Mohr hexahydrate. The sealed review's stronger early phrase "same stock" is qualified by its final root adjudication, which does not assert full composition equivalence.\n\nThe separate W02-F-PREPARATIONS DSMZ375/1107 cysteine overlap is a second family dependency under1201. Keep375's unknown strength/solvent/filtration distinct from1107's explicit5%w/v scope; do not create a chemically disjoint owner solely because source numbers differ. These exact families were not present in the previously sealed1237 family packet (ignored-inclusive comparison); this comment adds scope without duplicating its common identity rule.\n''')
put('comment-873.md',ctx+'''W02-F-FERRIC-CAS and W02-F-FERRIC-AVAILABILITY add two bounded follow-ups while retaining this issue's competing UNMAPPED_0385 owner.\n\nThe selected variable-hydrate payload says no own CAS is verified. [Fujifilm Wako](https://labchem-wako.fujifilm.com/us/product/detail/W01W0109-0283.html) explicitly pairs CAS15244-10-7 with Fe2(SO4)3·nH2O (captured SHA256 `59cf8f48daa8ad28ea509bed1997c9e4fa390ce85be2997a35761c7f5b1b8c9a`). Assess this registry scope and all existing-owner collisions under§3 before choosing identity; the supplier page does not prove each historical lot, fixed n, assay or original procurement. CHEBI131387's monohydrate must not replace variable hydration by exact identity.\n\nCase124's successful JCM413→369 and603→592 modification/base chains also need correct availability accounting. Do not treat available recipes as unavailable or confuse access with settled reagent/quantity identity. Preserve the existing rejected malformed ferric formula, all independently supported new spellings, competing-owner history and all release holds.\n\n'''+table(['w02-v2-ferric-variable-composed'])+'''\nNo owner winner, merge or new fixed chemistry is selected by this comment. The full source/registry conclusion and corrected exact payload must be independently re-reviewed.\n''')
put('comment-1229.md',ctx+'''W02-F-INHERITED-ALIASES contains additional exact form/product-scope obligations. Keep them distinct from already fixed selected aliases and from metadata that native policy already filters.\n\n| Owner | Literal/field | Required bounded disposition |\n|---|---|---|\n| Coso4.yaml | `cobalt(2+) sulfate--water (1/7)` RAW_TEXT | Exact seven-water name on anhydrous identity; preserve nonresolving provenance or supply a claim-specific alternate justification without merging owners. |\n| Cobalt_chloride_hexahydrate.yaml | `Cobalt(II) chloride--water (1/7)` EXACT_SYNONYM | Seven waters conflict with exact hexahydrate; assess/retire this exact claim, not all cobalt names. |\n| Mncl2_X_4_H2o.yaml | `MnCl4 x4H2O`, `MnCl4・4H2O` RAW_TEXT | Wrong chloride count requires original source/history correction evidence; do not invent a universal formula-normalization rule. |\n| Feso4_X_H2o.yaml | `Feromax`, `Fespan` EXACT_SYNONYM | ChEBI75834 explicitly records related BRAND NAME scope. Name import alone does not establish full commercial product equivalence to neat monohydrate. Supply exact evidence or preserve as nonresolving provenance. |\n\nRelated W02 scopes remain on their exact trackers: Sodium_Malate generic/fragment strings under811/868; Mohr generic/bare formula and vanadyl's related `vanadic sulfate pentahydrate` under1220; ammonium nickel duplicate form decision under1050; concentration strings under1230. Existing REJECTED tombstones are not active identity winners and must not be revived.\n\nThe coordinator re-ran actual native policies: 27 inspected Role:/Properties: strings are excluded by both MIM and Claw. They are optional classification cleanup, not a present resolver leak. `a-proposal-anhydrous-alum` already rejects `Na SiO .9H O` and `ZnSO .7H O`;811's existing exact correction comment remains valid, so do not repeat those changes or reopen them as an uncorrected successor defect. Supported source-proven raw spelling corrections remain admissible under§3; no blanket rejection of missing hydrate qualifiers is authorized.\n''')
put('comment-1230.md',ctx+'''W02-F-INHERITED-ALIASES / w02-external-b-010 adds two concentration-label contexts. `Nh42ni_So42_X_6_H2o.yaml` retains `(NH4)2Ni(SO4)2 x6H2O (0.1%w/v)` as HYDRATE_FORM; its bare double-salt sibling also retains the stock text. Keep the supported nickel-stock preparation separate from neat solute and preserve1050's unresolved generic-owner form/merge decision. Do not repair by choosing a namespace or merging the two owners.\n\n`P-aminobenzoic_Acid.yaml` retains `pABA (0.3 µg/µL)` as an identity-bearing label. Its original stock-versus-dose context is not established: do not call it a proven stock or manufacture a preparation merely because a concentration is printed. Recover and assess source scope, retaining literal/history and withholding unsupported global alias approval. The independently confirmed ABEE ethyl-ester conflict is separate and has its own proposed tracker.\n\n'''+table(['b-proposal-paba','w02-proposal-ammonium-nickel-hexahydrate'])+'''\nThe relevant native policy admits these literals; eligibility is not scientific equivalence. Preserve all existing source and release holds and independently review the exact successor.\n''')
put('comment-718.md',ctx+'''Qualified W02-F-INHERITED-ALIASES / w02-external-b-013 role/citation disposition: the selected corpus still contains provisional computational roles and incomplete role evidence. Native evidence-gap accounting on the106 selected payloads finds seven prediction-only role assertions and one role without evidence. Those are unapproved claims to retain/review, not proof that predicted roles are chemically false; do not delete or promote them merely to obtain a clean whole-owner verdict.\n\nThe water mapping's PMID36233206 is explicitly auto-proposed context (distilled-water control in a collagen/mouse experiment); PABA PMID31986050 concerns a ketoconazole/PABA cocrystal. Neither abstract alone establishes exact-owner identity or functional-role applicability. Assess claim-specific use and evidence placement; do not relabel genuine contextual mentions as nonexistent source text. Preserve evidence/historical context and keep unsupported scientific approvals withheld.\n\nNative Role:/Properties: strings are already filtered (27 inspected exact strings tested in both MIM and Claw), and agar SINGLE_INGREDIENT is explicitly allowed by the schema. These are not present resolver leaks or an agar typing defect. No new role approval, gate or schema change is requested. The native review's whole-owner holds remain independently tracked, including SEM:db276e2e3eae5d2442dc and retained partial SEM obligations.\n''')
